    1. Choose grid H (6-9), W (6-9); pick 3 colors for bg, barrier, moving
    2. Decide 1-2 moving groups; for each, pick group_height (2-4) and run_len (1-2); assign row ranges (non-overlapping, separated by >=1 non-moving row)
    3. For each moving row, choose a target_start position (0 or barrier_col+1); place barrier pixels to the left of target_start randomly; place the moving run at [target_start, target_start+run_len-1] -- this is the OUTPUT
    4. Scatter barrier pixels in non-moving rows (density ~0.3-0.4), ensuring every non-moving row has >=1 barrier
    5. Verify at least one moving row has slide>0 (target_start < W-run_len); if not, adjust
    6. Derive INPUT: move each run from its output position to the right edge [W-run_len, W-1], filling vacated cells with bg; ensure no barrier occupies right-edge columns in moving rows
